{"cuisine/raramuri-foodways":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/raramuri-foodways","n":"Rarámuri foodways","c":"#94bd5c","crumb":[["The Americas","cuisines#the-americas"],["Native American cuisine","cuisine/native-american-cuisine"]],"sub":"Indigenous foodways, Sierra Tarahumara, Chihuahua, Mexico","names":"Rarámuri","intro":[[["Corn","ingredient/maize"]," is the most important crop for the Rarámuri of the Sierra Tarahumara, grown in family plots and milpas. Popped and ground, it becomes ",["Pinole","dish/pinole"]," and esquiate. Many children now eat industrial meals at boarding schools, so the Rarámuri group NATIKA asked researchers from UNAM to film families making these foods, to help bring them back to the table."],["Families live far apart in the mountains, and ",["Tesgüino","dish/tesguino"],", a thick corn beer the Rarámuri call sowiki, brings them together. Women sprout the corn, grind it, boil it for hours and ferment it in clay pots, and when the pots are opened it's first offered to Onorúame, the Father. It's shared at gatherings for healing, births and deaths, planting and harvest, ball races and house building, after the men have worked the host's fields together."]],"src":"note","sources":[{"name":"Society of Ethnobiology, Documentation of traditional foods and agrobiodiversity of the Rarámuri (Linares, Bye and Mera, UNAM)","url":"https://ethnobiology.org/conference/abstracts/40/documentation-traditional-foods-and-agrobiodiversity-rar-muri-chihuahua"},{"name":"La Jornada del Campo, Sowiki, la bebida rarámuri","url":"https://www.jornada.com.mx/2015/05/16/cam-bebida.html"}],"actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"raramuri-foodways"}],"sections":[{"h":"Dishes","count":2,"links":[["Pinole","dish/pinole"],["Tesgüino","dish/tesguino"]]},{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Native American cuisine","cuisine/native-american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Maize","ingredient/maize"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Native American cuisine","cuisine/native-american-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Cuisine of the Americas","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/4/49/Milk%2C_machica_%28in_bag%29_and_pinol_mix_%28in_tin%29.jpg/500px-Milk%2C_machica_%28in_bag%29_and_pinol_mix_%28in_tin%29.jpg","w":500,"h":399,"by":"GrammarFascist","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Milk%2C_machica_(in_bag)_and_pinol_mix_(in_tin).jpg","of":"Pinole"}},"ingredient/pecorino":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/pecorino","n":"Pecorino","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 2 dishes across 2 cuisines","intro":[["Pecorino is an Italian hard cheese produced from sheep's milk. The name pecorino derives from pecora, which means 'sheep' in Italian."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-pecorino"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pecorino"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine",[["Carbonara","dish/carbonara"],["Rafanata","dish/rafanata"]]],["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Carbonara","dish/carbonara"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Black pepper","ingredient/black-pepper"],["Guanciale","ingredient/guanciale"],["Pancetta","ingredient/pancetta"],["Pasta","ingredient/pasta"],["Pecorino romano","ingredient/pecorino-romano"],["Peppercorn","ingredient/peppercorn"],["Spaghetti","ingredient/spaghetti"],["Extra virgin olive oil","ingredient/extra-virgin-olive-oil"],["Horseradish","ingredient/horseradish"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/8/83/A_Pecorino_cheese_plate_at_Hong_Kong.jpg/500px-A_Pecorino_cheese_plate_at_Hong_Kong.jpg","w":500,"h":750,"by":"Peachyeung316","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_Pecorino_cheese_plate_at_Hong_Kong.jpg"}},"dish/cilok":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/cilok","n":"Cilok","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Indonesian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Cilok is an Indonesian ball-shaped dumpling made from aci (tapioca starch), a Sundanese snack originated from Indonesia. In Sundanese, cilok is an abbreviation of aci dicolok or \"poked tapioca\", since the tapioca balls are poked with lidi skewers made from the midrib of the coconut palm frond."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-cilok"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cilok"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Peanut sauce","ingredient/peanut-sauce"],["Sambal","ingredient/sambal"],["Tapioca","ingredient/tapioca"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Daily Cooking Quest","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dailycookingquest.com","note":"Indonesian home cook Anita's blog with a large archive of Indonesian recipes.","url":"https://dailycookingquest.com/cuisines/indonesian.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Indonesian cuisine","links":[["Arem-arem","dish/arem-arem"],["Arsik","dish/arsik"],["Asam pedas","dish/asam-pedas"],["Ayam goreng","dish/ayam-goreng"],["Ayam goreng kalasan","dish/ayam-goreng-kalasan"],["Ayam panggang","dish/ayam-panggang"],["Ayam Taliwang","dish/ayam-taliwang"],["Bajigur","dish/bajigur"],["Bakakak hayam","dish/bakakak-hayam"],["Bakpia","dish/bakpia"],["Bakwan","dish/bakwan"],["Bekasang","dish/bekasang"],["Betutu","dish/betutu"],["Bika ambon","dish/bika-ambon"],["Binte biluhuta","dish/binte-biluhuta"],["Bir pletok","dish/bir-pletok"],["Bolu kukus","dish/bolu-kukus"],["Botok","dish/botok"],["Brem","dish/brem"],["Bubur kacang hijau","dish/bubur-kacang-hijau"],["Bubur ketan hitam","dish/bubur-ketan-hitam"],["Bubur pedas","dish/bubur-pedas"],["Bunti