"page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mont-blanc_P1020796.jpg"}},"dish/pastilla":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/pastilla","n":"Pastilla","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Moroccan cuisine","dot":"#e46a3f","intro":[["Pastilla is a meat or seafood pie in Maghrebi cuisine made with warqa dough (ورقة), which is similar to filo. It is a specialty of Morocco, Algeria, and Tunisia, where its variation is known as malsouka. It has more recently been spread by emigrants to France, Israel, and North America."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-pastilla"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pastilla"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Moroccan cuisine","cuisine/moroccan-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":5,"links":[["Broth","ingredient/broth"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Fish","ingredient/fish"],["Offal","ingredient/offal"],["Squab","ingredient/squab"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"My Moroccan Food","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"mymoroccanfood.com","note":"Moroccan recipe blog linked to cookbook author Nargisse Benkabbou, covering breads, soups and tagines.","url":"https://www.mymoroccanfood.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Taste of Maroc","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"tasteofmaroc.com","note":"Moroccan recipes and tutorials from Christine Benlafquih, formerly the Moroccan food writer at The Spruce Eats.","url":"https://tasteofmaroc.com/about/","suggested":true,"kind":"site"},{"name":"Salima's Kitchen","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"salimaskitchen.com","note":"Moroccan section of Salima Benkhalti's blog, drawing on her family cooking.","url":"https://salimaskitchen.com/category/moroccan/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Moroccan cuisine","links":[["Babbouche","dish/babbouche"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Couscous","dish/couscous"],["Harira","dish/harira"],["Kourdass","dish/kourdass"],["Medfouna","dish/medfouna"